## Instructions

This is review round {{.Round}} of at most {{.MaxRounds}}.

Judge the change against the task and the acceptance criteria. Report the defects a maintainer would ask to have fixed before merging: wrong behavior, an unmet requirement, a missing test for new behavior, a security or data-loss risk, an unhandled error. Do not report style preferences.

Each finding has:
- "severity": "high" for wrong behavior, an unmet requirement, a security or data-loss risk; "medium" for a real defect of limited reach or a missing test; "low" for a minor defect still worth fixing.
- "claim": one sentence that states the defect and where it is.
- "location": optional, a file path with an optional line number, such as "internal/foo/bar.go:42".

The verdict is "approve" when nothing must change before merging, and "changes_requested" when at least one finding must be fixed. A "changes_requested" verdict lists at least one finding. An "approve" verdict may list low-severity findings as notes; they are not sent back to the author.

Answer with a single JSON object and nothing else, no prose and no code fences, in exactly this shape:
{"verdict": "changes_requested", "findings": [{"severity": "high", "claim": "...", "location": "..."}], "summary": "one sentence"}
